(## 5. Explain JWT In The Project) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Question) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Explain JWT in the project. How is it used and what is the real working of it?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Answer) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(JWT is used as a signed login token. After successful login, the backend gives a token to) Tj
T*
(the frontend. The frontend sends this token with every protected API request.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### JWT Login Flow) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```text) Tj
T*
(User enters email and password) Tj
T*
(    |) Tj
T*
(Frontend calls POST /api/auth/login) Tj
T*
(    |) Tj
T*
(AuthController validates credentials) Tj
T*
(    |) Tj
T*
(JwtUtils generates token) Tj
T*
(    |) Tj
T*
(Frontend stores token in localStorage) Tj
T*
(    |) Tj
T*
(Every protected request sends Authorization: Bearer <token>) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### JWT Content) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In the project, token is generated using:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```java) Tj
T*
(jwtUtils.generateToken\(user.getEmail\(\), user.getId\(\), user.getRole\(\)\);) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The token contains:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```json) Tj
T*
({) Tj
T*
(  "sub": "user@email.com",) Tj
T*
(  "user_id": 5,) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
