(  "role": "CUSTOMER",) Tj
T*
(  "iat": "issued time",) Tj
T*
(  "exp": "expiry time") Tj
T*
(}) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Frontend Usage) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In `utils/api.js`, Axios adds the token:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```js) Tj
T*
(config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Backend Validation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(`CustomJwtFilter`:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Reads the `Authorization` header.) Tj
T*
(- Extracts the token after `Bearer`.) Tj
T*
(- Extracts email from token.) Tj
T*
(- Loads user from database.) Tj
T*
(- Validates token signature and expiry.) Tj
T*
(- Sets authentication in Spring Security context.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Role Authorization) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(`SecurityConfiguration` protects APIs:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(```java) Tj
T*
(.requestMatchers\("/api/admin/**"\).hasRole\("ADMIN"\)) Tj
T*
(.requestMatchers\("/api/customer/**"\).hasRole\("CUSTOMER"\)) Tj
T*
(.requestMatchers\("/api/provider/**"\).hasRole\("SERVICEPROVIDER"\)) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Short Interview Answer) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(JWT is used for stateless authentication. After login, the backend generates a signed token) Tj
T*
(containing email, user id, role, issue time, and expiry. The frontend stores it and sends it) Tj
T*
(in the Authorization header. The backend validates it in a custom JWT filter and Spring) Tj
T*
(Security uses the role to protect admin, customer, and provider APIs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(---) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
